{"tool_name":"ukbpheno","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"ukbpheno","home":"https://github.com/niekverw/ukbpheno","license":"MIT","summary":"An R package for phenotyping health-related outcomes in the UK Biobank.","addition_date":"2022-08-29T10:27:46.341136Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-24T15:45:35.753730Z","tool_type":["Library"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:ukbpheno","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"m.w.yeung@umcg.nl","name":"Ming Wai Yeung","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9794-3109","typeEntity":"Person"},{"email":"n.verweij@umcg.nl","name":"Niek Verweij","typeEntity":"Person"},{"name":"Pim van der Harst"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Regression analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3659"},{"term":"Standardisation and normalisation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3435"},{"term":"Visualisation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0337"}]}],"name":"ukbpheno","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"Jennifer","publication":[{"doi":"10.1016/j.xpro.2022.101471","metadata":{"abstract":"The complexity and volume of data associated with population-based cohorts means that generating health-related outcomes can be challenging. Using one such cohort, the UK Biobank\u2014a major open access resource\u2014we present a protocol to efficiently integrate the main dataset and record-level data files, to harmonize and process the data using an R package named \u201cukbpheno\u201d. We describe how to use the package to generate binary phenotypes in a standardized and machine-actionable manner. For complete details on the use and execution of this protocol, please refer to Yeung et al. (2022).","authors":[{"name":"Verweij N."},{"name":"Yeung M.W."},{"name":"van der Harst P."}],"citationCount":6,"date":"2022-09-16T00:00:00Z","journal":"STAR Protocols","title":"ukbpheno v1.0: An R package for phenotyping heal